# A reference to a law with its parameter values (alice_lol::law_ref)
law alice_law_ref_v1
kind layout
claim a law reference is a 72-byte header naming the law and the semantics it was written under, then one 40-byte row per parameter of the law, in the law's declared order, and nothing after
claim a row's name is the parameter's name followed by zero bytes up to 32 bytes; its value is the bits of an IEEE binary64 number
source alice-lol/src/law_ref.rs (module documentation)

endian le

const MAGIC bytes = 0x4c4f4c52
const VERSION integer = 1
const MAX_PARAMS integer = 64

block header size 72
field magic bytes 4 = MAGIC refuse bad_magic
field version u16 = VERSION refuse version
field count u16 in 0 MAX_PARAMS refuse count
field semantics_id bytes 32
field law_id bytes 32
end block

block param size 40
field name bytes 32
field value u64
end block

segment header block header refuse too_short
segment params table param count header.count refuse layout
